# Mobile-First Design

Most visitors will use smartphones. Default to mobile layouts and enhance for larger screens.

## CSS

- Write base styles for small screens; use `@media (min-width: …)` to scale up.
- Breakpoints: `640px` (tablet), `960px` (desktop).
- Use spacing and sizing tokens from `index.css` (`--space-*`, `--touch-target`, `--font-size-*`).
- Touch targets must be at least 44px (`var(--touch-target)`).
- Body text must stay at 16px (`1rem`) minimum to avoid iOS input zoom.
- Account for notched devices with `env(safe-area-inset-*)`.

## Components

- Prefer stacked, full-width layouts on mobile.
- Make navigation and CTAs easy to tap with one thumb.
- Test narrow viewports (~320px) before adding desktop-only patterns.
- Avoid hover-only interactions; ensure touch and keyboard access.

## Example

```css
/* Mobile base */
.card {
  padding: var(--space-md);
}

/* Enhance for tablet+ */
@media (min-width: 640px) {
  .card {
    padding: var(--space-lg);
  }
}
```
